// The environment (M6 Task 10).
//
// `getenv(name)` is a builtin, not a function in this module: the name lives in
// the one shared scope, so a wrapper would be a duplicate definition. It answers
// `Option[string]`: `Some(value)` when the variable is set -- an empty variable
// is `Some("")` -- and `None` when it is not. The two cases used to read the same
// empty string; they are different answers and now different values.
//
// Ownership: the argument is borrowed and the result's string is owned.
